        </div><div class="article-template__content page-width page-width--narrow rte scroll-trigger animate--slide-in">
          <div class="rocket-shopify-article lngvty-article" style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;color:#181818;font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,'Century Gothic','Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;letter-spacing:.15px;">

    <p style="max-width:760px;margin:0 0 24px;color:rgba(24,24,24,.68);font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;letter-spacing:.2px;">
        On the face, a vitamin C serum does three things: it works as an antioxidant, it supports collagen, and it helps stop new dark marks from forming, and each of those effects builds over weeks to months.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:0 0 38px;padding:20px 22px;border-left:4px solid #181818;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            <strong style="font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.5px;">Quick answer:</strong>
            Applied to the face, vitamin C neutralises some of the oxidative stress that daily sun exposure creates, supports collagen, and slows pigment formation so tone looks more even over time. These changes build over weeks to months and work best alongside daily sunscreen. A vitamin C serum is not an instant brightener, and it does not replace sunscreen or clear deep pigmentation quickly.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Vitamin C is one of the most popular ingredients in skincare, and one of the most overpromised. It is a real, well-studied ingredient with a defined job description, and knowing that job description makes it easier to decide whether you need it and what to expect.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        The three jobs vitamin C does on your face
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>It acts as an antioxidant.</strong> Vitamin C is one of the most powerful antioxidants in the skin. Reviews describe protection against photoaging, and a partnership with vitamin E that helps it protect against oxidative damage.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>It supports collagen.</strong> Skin naturally contains high concentrations of vitamin C, and it takes part in collagen synthesis.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28805671/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> In a six-month trial, healthy women with photoaged skin used a 5% vitamin C cream on one side and a plain base on the other. The treated side showed clinically visible improvement, with more skin relief and fewer deep furrows.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12823436/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>It slows pigment formation.</strong> Vitamin C reduces melanin formation.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> A meta-analysis of 31 small trials in 741 healthy volunteers found that vitamin C limited the pigmentation produced by simulated daylight, and that the effect grew with the dose.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30881584/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        These are all slow, protective jobs. Vitamin C works in the background to keep skin from getting worse and to make steady, modest improvements. It does not act like a filter.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What you will actually notice
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        The evidence points to patience. A systematic review of seven randomised trials found that vitamin C lightened pigmentation and made photoaged skin smoother and less wrinkled, but also noted that long-term use may be needed for noticeable change.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37128827/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a> The six-month cream trial above assessed skin after three and six months, not after days.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12823436/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        A realistic way to think about it:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks.</strong> Early signs, such as a fresher-looking tone, may begin to show, and new UV-driven marks are less likely to form.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30881584/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Months.</strong> Skin texture looks smoother and pigmentation lightens, as seen in the longer trials.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12823436/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37128827/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Always.</strong> The benefit depends on staying consistent and wearing sunscreen every morning.</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="margin:42px 0;padding:30px 26px;background:#181818;color:#FFFFFF;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2.2px;text-transform:uppercase;">
            The LNGVTY system
        </p>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:31px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.8px;">
            Choose by skin concern
        </h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 24px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">
            Dull, tight or dehydrated skin that you also want to look brighter points to the serum below.
        </p>

