    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Which kind of vitamin C?
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Vitamin C is a tricky ingredient to keep stable. Reviews describe finding a formula that is both stable and able to penetrate the skin as the main challenge, so the form matters as much as the amount.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> Derivatives of vitamin C are designed to be steadier than ascorbic acid itself.
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        <a href="/products/deep-hydration-glow-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum</a> uses a derivative, 3-O-ethyl ascorbic acid, a stable form of vitamin C chosen so that the glow builds gradually. Be aware that the trials above did not test this ingredient, so they show what vitamin C can do in general and do not prove the same results for this serum. The serum's own clinical study on Indian skin found that glow increased by 35.2% at four weeks, and individual results may vary.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        How to use a vitamin C serum on your face
    </h2>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Cleanse</strong> with a gentle cleanser.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Apply 3 to 4 drops on damp skin,</strong> across the whole face.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Moisturise</strong> to finish the step.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Wear sunscreen in the morning.</strong> Vitamin C supports sun protection, and it does not replace it.</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Patch test before first use, especially if your skin is reactive. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, check with a doctor first. The serum already contains vitamin C and niacinamide, so you do not need to add more actives alongside it.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            Pick one vitamin C product and use it consistently for at least a month before judging it. Switching serums every week makes it impossible to know what is working.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What vitamin C can and cannot do
    </h2>

    <div style="margin:24px 0 34px;overflow-x:auto;border-top:2px solid #181818;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);">
        <table style="width:100%;min-width:620px;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
